498
00:39:58,256 --> 00:40:00,056
Welcome to...

499
00:40:00,104 --> 00:40:03,904
ベンジマイト・コンコクションズ！イェーイ！
Bae-gemite Concoctions! Yeah!

500
00:40:13,104 --> 00:40:16,904
見てる方も I think everyone knows, 一応自己紹介お願いしていいですか？
For those watching... I think everyone knows, but could you please introduce yourselves?

501
00:40:17,004 --> 00:40:18,604
はい！もちろんでございます！じゃあ私から！
Yes! Of course! Well then, I'll go first!

502
00:40:18,704 --> 00:40:23,704
ホロスターズの夕刻ロベルでーす！本日よろしくお願いします！
I'm Yukoku Roberu from Holostars! It's great to be here today!

503
00:40:23,904 --> 00:40:27,604
なんか不穏な感じがね、しますけど。
Though I have a bad feeling about this...

504
00:40:27,904 --> 00:40:30,104
そうですね。はい、怖いです。
Indeed. Yes, I'm scared.

505
00:40:30,104 --> 00:40:33,104
怖くない... あ、怖くないもんね！
You're not scared... Oh, right, you're not!

506
00:40:33,104 --> 00:40:35,604
頑張りたいと思います！よろしくお願いします！
I'll do my best! Nice to be here!

507
00:40:35,704 --> 00:40:36,604
そして！
And next!

508
00:40:36,604 --> 00:40:41,104
はい。あの... 理由も分からず呼び出されて、仕事だと思って来たら...
Yes. Um... I was called over without knowing why, thinking it was regular work...

509
00:40:41,204 --> 00:40:47,104
なんだか不穏なスタジオでした。石川界人です！声優です！よろしくお願いします！
But I found myself in a very sketchy studio. I'm Kaito Ishikawa, a voice actor! Pleasure to be here!

510
00:40:48,404 --> 00:40:51,104
そんな我々からも、ちょっとベーちゃんに言わなきゃいけないことあります！
From the two of us, there's something we have to tell you, Bae-chan!

511
00:40:51,104 --> 00:40:53,104
ありますね！じゃあ行きましょう！はい！
Oh, absolutely! Alright, let's do it! Ready!

512
00:40:53,104 --> 00:41:00,104
せーの！ソロライブ開催決定、おめでとう！
Ready, set... Congratulations on your upcoming solo live!

513
00:41:00,204 --> 00:41:02,904
ありがとうございます！
Thank you so much!

514
00:41:03,104 --> 00:41:08,104
あ、泣いちゃった！あらららら！嬉しいな！いや、すごいことよ！おめでとう！
Ah, she's crying! Oh my goodness! How sweet! Truly an amazing achievement! Congrats!

515
00:41:08,304 --> 00:41:12,104
本当にありがとうございます！本当におめでとう！
Thank you so, so much! Big congratulations!

516
00:41:12,104 --> 00:41:18,604
一VTuberファンとしてさ... ソロライブっていうのは夢じゃん！
As a fellow VTuber fan... A solo live is the ultimate dream!

517
00:41:18,704 --> 00:41:21,104
夢ですよ！本当に！
It really is a dream come true!

518
00:41:21,204 --> 00:41:24,604
なんかもう、熱いわー！
Wow, I'm getting all emotional here!

519
00:41:24,904 --> 00:41:26,604
本当に素晴らしい！
It's truly wonderful!

520
00:41:26,704 --> 00:41:30,604
えーっと、今日はね、チャレンジをやりたいと思います！
Well then, today we're going to do a challenge!

521
00:41:30,704 --> 00:41:33,604
チャレンジ！いいですね、挑戦！
A challenge! Sounds great!

522
00:41:33,704 --> 00:41:42,104
Today we've invited these two for a challenge called The Bae-gemite Concoctions.

523
00:41:42,204 --> 00:41:46,904
まぁ、ロベルさんと界人さんは、もうベンジマイトの事ご存知でいらっしゃいますよね？
Well, Roberu-san and Kaito-san, you both already know all about Vegemite, right?

524
00:41:47,004 --> 00:41:51,104
当たり前のように口にしてるけど... 我々にとっては...
You say that so casually, but for us...

525
00:41:51,204 --> 00:41:57,904
我々にとっては、その... 呪いみたいなもんだから！その、怖いのよ結構！
For us, it's pretty much like a curse! Honestly, it's quite terrifying!

526
00:41:58,004 --> 00:42:02,904
ベンジマイトと言ったらロベルさんですよね？
When you think Vegemite, you think Roberu-san, right?

527
00:42:03,104 --> 00:42:08,604
正直このベンジマイトという道を作ってしまった発端の人物かも知れない。
To be honest, I might be the origin of this whole Vegemite madness.

528
00:42:08,704 --> 00:42:15,604
ベーちゃんにベンジマイトって物があるよって教えてもらって、僕が実食配信みたいなのをするようになったんですよ。
Bae-chan told me about Vegemite, and I ended up doing a taste-test stream.

529
00:42:15,704 --> 00:42:22,604
そこから始まったこの地獄は。多分。そして被害者たちが生まれて行った。
That's probably where this hell started, spawning a chain of new victims.

530
00:42:22,704 --> 00:42:28,904
そう、で、一緒に配信で食レポみたいな配信もしたことがあって。
Yeah, and we even did a stream together doing food reviews on it.

531
00:42:29,004 --> 00:42:34,604
それ以来なんで、こいつと対峙するのは3、4年ぶりくらいになりますかね、まあ。
So facing off against this stuff again... It's been about 3 or 4 years now.

532
00:42:34,704 --> 00:42:37,104
じゃあもう味も忘れちゃってそうだもんね。
So you've probably forgotten the taste by now then?

533
00:42:37,204 --> 00:42:42,604
うん、あのね... こびり付いてる。4年経っても消えない。味の記憶がこびり付いてる！
Well, you see... It's burned into my mind. Even after 4 years, the memory of that taste remains burned into my brain!

534
00:42:42,904 --> 00:42:48,604
だから非常に怖さはあるけど、まあでもね、楽しみですよ。
So I'm pretty scared, but at the same time, I'm looking forward to it.

535
00:42:48,704 --> 00:42:51,604
もっと元気そうに！楽しみです！イエーイ！
Say it with more energy! "I'm looking forward to it! Yeah!"

536
00:42:51,704 --> 00:42:54,904
すごい楽しみ！食べたい！
I'm super excited! Can't wait to eat it!

537
00:42:55,004 --> 00:42:58,604
そして界人さん！あの、ベンジマイトエピソードっていうことはありますか？
And Kaito-san! Do you have any Vegemite episodes or stories?

538
00:42:58,704 --> 00:43:04,104
あー、ベンジマイトエピソードですか？非常に素晴らしい食材ですよね。
Ah, a Vegemite story? Well, it's a truly wonderful ingredient, isn't it?

539
00:43:04,204 --> 00:43:11,604
もらってましたよね？ベーちゃんから。ホロごえで一緒になった時に、ベーちゃんからありがたいお土産をもらってましたよね？
You got some, right? From Bae-chan. When you appeared together on Hologoe, you got a lovely souvenir from her, right?

540
00:43:11,704 --> 00:43:16,904
ええ。番組収録終了時にね、わざわざ楽屋にご挨拶いただいて...
Yes. After we finished recording the show, she came all the way to my green room to greet me...

541
00:43:17,004 --> 00:43:22,604
なんて丁寧な方なんだろうと。素敵な方だなと思って、受け取って「これお土産です」と。
I thought, "What a polite and wonderful person!" She handed it to me and said, "This is a souvenir for you."

542
00:43:22,704 --> 00:43:28,104
「ありがとうございます！あれですか？何かお菓子か何かですか？」「あ、ベンジマイトです」
I said, "Thank you so much! Is it snacks or something?" She replied, "Ah, it's Vegemite."

543
00:43:33,104 --> 00:43:37,604
一応食べましたよ。おー偉い！食べました！？ちゃんと食べました。
I did eat it, by the way. / Oh, good boy! You ate it?! / Yes, I made sure to eat it.

544
00:43:38,104 --> 00:43:42,604
なんて素晴らしい食材なんだろうって思いましたね！
I thought to myself, "What an incredible ingredient this is!"

545
00:43:42,704 --> 00:43:47,904
素晴らしいんだ、やっぱり！ベンジマイトというのは！ベンジマイト素晴らしいです！
So it really is amazing after all! Vegemite is! / Vegemite is wonderful!

546
00:43:48,004 --> 00:43:53,904
ちょっとね、記憶もあんまないと思いますので、ちょっと先、生で食べさせてもらいます！
Since you might not remember the exact taste, first, you're going to try it raw!

547
00:43:54,004 --> 00:43:58,904
I gotta refresh their memories on the taste, so we do have Vegemite prepared in front of us.

548
00:43:59,004 --> 00:44:04,604
大丈夫？いや、大丈夫じゃないです！お願いってわけじゃなくて...
Are you sure? / Well, it's not fine! And it's not a request...

549
00:44:04,704 --> 00:44:09,604
5周年なんで... 命令です！食え！
Since it's my 5th anniversary... it's an order! EAT IT!

550
00:44:10,104 --> 00:44:16,904
ソロライブも決まってるしな！そんなおめでたい人の命令じゃー！
Plus her solo live was just announced! How can I refuse an order from someone celebrating!

551
00:44:17,004 --> 00:44:19,904
そうです！じゃあみんな... あ、怖い！
That's right! Alright everyone... Ah, terrifying!

552
00:44:20,104 --> 00:44:25,604
せーの！乾杯！乾杯！
Ready, set... Cheers! / Cheers!

553
00:44:26,104 --> 00:44:29,604
んー！美味っ！
Mmm! Delicious!

554
00:44:34,104 --> 00:44:35,904
うわ、美味しい！
Wow, yummy!

555
00:44:36,104 --> 00:44:40,104
美味ーい！美味いね！すっごい！
Yummy! So good, right?! Incredible!

556
00:44:40,204 --> 00:44:44,104
大丈夫ですか？
Are you okay?

557
00:44:44,604 --> 00:44:48,104
大丈夫じゃなさそ... え！もう飲み切っちゃいました！
Doesn't look okay... Wait! He already finished the whole bottle of water!

558
00:44:48,204 --> 00:44:53,604
Ishikawa Kaito has finished one bottle of water. えっーと、早いっすね！
Ishikawa Kaito has finished one bottle of water. Wow, that was fast!

559
00:44:53,704 --> 00:44:57,104
うわぁ... お水にとっても合うなぁ！
Whoa... It goes so remarkably well with water!

560
00:45:00,119 --> 00:45:01,419
ああ、幸せ〜
Ah, bliss...

561
00:45:01,419 --> 00:45:03,419
ああ〜
Ahhh...

562
00:45:03,419 --> 00:45:07,519
大丈夫でしょうか？ちょっとあの、ロベル先輩の顔がえぐいっす。
Is everything okay? Um, Roberu-senpai's face looks intense.

563
00:45:08,919 --> 00:45:10,019
泣いてる。
He's crying.

564
00:45:10,019 --> 00:45:11,019
泣いてます？
Is he crying?

565
00:45:11,019 --> 00:45:12,419
ほぼ泣いてる。
He's practically crying.

566
00:45:12,419 --> 00:45:13,419
なんで？
Why?

567
00:45:13,419 --> 00:45:14,619
美味し...
Delicious...

568
00:45:14,619 --> 00:45:16,119
美味しすぎて？
Because it's too delicious?

569
00:45:16,119 --> 00:45:17,419
美味しすぎてね...
It's too delicious...

570
00:45:17,419 --> 00:45:19,519
Everybody is crying.

571
00:45:19,519 --> 00:45:21,119
涙が止まらないね。
The tears won't stop.

572
00:45:21,119 --> 00:45:25,119
ちょっとあの、進行役の... 多分両端死んでる。
Wait, the hosts... both ends are probably dead.

573
00:45:25,119 --> 00:45:27,319
多分両端死んでると思って。
I thought both ends were dead.

574
00:45:27,319 --> 00:45:28,219
はい。
Right.

575
00:45:28,219 --> 00:45:29,719
はい、じゃあ説明行きます。
Okay, let's move on to the explanation.

576
00:45:29,719 --> 00:45:36,919
We have the Vegemite Concoctions! So it is a tasting competition... I mean, tasting event.

577
00:45:36,919 --> 00:45:44,819
To explain how it works, before today, Roberu-senpai, A-san, and I each came up with an ingredient that we thought would pair well with Vegemite.

578
00:45:44,819 --> 00:45:52,719
And using all of our ideas as inspiration, a professional food coordinator... プロ!
And using all of our ideas as inspiration, a professional food coordinator... Professional!

579
00:45:52,719 --> 00:45:54,119
えー！あ、そう！
Eh?! Ah, really?!

580
00:45:54,119 --> 00:46:03,119
...professional food coordinator has created each dish with great care, and we're going to taste all of them and decide who came up with the best Vegemite Concoction!

581
00:46:03,119 --> 00:46:06,119
なるほど。我々が選んだ食材でプロの方が...
I see. With the ingredients we picked, a professional...

582
00:46:06,119 --> 00:46:10,919
すごく美味しくベジマイトを使って料理してくださってると。
has cooked them to be super delicious using Vegemite.

583
00:46:10,919 --> 00:46:11,919
はい！
Yes!

584
00:46:11,919 --> 00:46:12,819
なるほど。
I see.

585
00:46:12,819 --> 00:46:14,019
これ信じられるの？
Can we really believe this?

586
00:46:14,019 --> 00:46:16,519
いや、でもベジマイトって元々美味しいので...
Well, Vegemite is already delicious to begin with...

587
00:46:16,519 --> 00:46:17,919
あ、そうだった。ごめんごめん。プロだからね。
Ah, that's right. Sorry, sorry. Since they're professionals.

588
00:46:17,919 --> 00:46:19,519
プロだもんね。
They're professionals after all.

589
00:46:19,519 --> 00:46:21,419
ベジマイト美味しいしね。
And Vegemite is tasty anyway.

590
00:46:21,419 --> 00:46:25,119
なので、まあ美味しいプラス美味しいイコール美味しいじゃないですか。
So, tasty plus tasty equals tasty, right?

591
00:46:25,119 --> 00:46:26,219
ああ、そうですね。美味しい。
Ah, that's true. Tasty.

592
00:46:26,219 --> 00:46:27,619
美味しい。美味しい。
Tasty. Tasty.

593
00:46:27,619 --> 00:46:31,019
ということで、あの、お互い何を選んだか全く分かんない。
So, none of us know at all what the others chose.

594
00:46:31,019 --> 00:46:35,019
We don't know what the other has chosen, so it's going to be a surprise to us as well.

595
00:46:35,019 --> 00:46:36,619
まぁ、早速始めようか。
Well, shall we get started right away?

596
00:46:36,619 --> 00:46:38,319
あ、なるほど。始めます？
Ah, I see. Shall we start?

597
00:46:38,319 --> 00:46:40,019
いいですよ。始めます？
Sounds good. Shall we begin?

598
00:46:40,019 --> 00:46:42,619
一旦休憩時間欲しいかな？
Can I get a break real quick?

599
00:46:42,619 --> 00:46:44,319
休憩？
A break?

600
00:46:44,319 --> 00:46:48,119
胃の中でベジマイトが大暴れしてるんだわ。
Vegemite is rampaging inside my stomach.

601
00:46:48,119 --> 00:46:51,019
うん、すごいよね。生きてる、これは。
Yeah, it's intense. It's alive, this stuff.

602
00:46:51,019 --> 00:46:55,719
まあ、最初ちょっと何を言ったか...選んだか、ロベ先輩に聞きたくて...
Well, first I'd like to ask Roberu-senpai what he chose...

603
00:46:55,719 --> 00:46:57,719
じゃあ僕から行きますか。
Shall I go first then?

604
00:46:57,719 --> 00:46:58,919
最初にお願いします。
First, please go ahead.

605
00:46:58,919 --> 00:47:04,019
わかりました。えーでは僕が選んだ食材はこちらでございます！
Understood. Well, the ingredient I chose is this right here!

606
00:47:04,019 --> 00:47:06,319
牛タンです！
Beef tongue!

607
00:47:06,319 --> 00:47:08,619
おー！
Ooh!

608
00:47:08,619 --> 00:47:11,119
神！牛タンです！
God tier! It's beef tongue!

609
00:47:11,119 --> 00:47:13,719
いいね！しょっぱいじゃないですか、ベジマイトって。
Nice! Isn't Vegemite salty?

610
00:47:13,719 --> 00:47:16,419
うんうん。で、これはお肉に合うんじゃないかなと思ったんですよ、僕。
Yeah, yeah. So I thought this would pair well with meat.

611
00:47:16,419 --> 00:47:18,519
おー！
Ooh!

612
00:47:18,519 --> 00:47:22,519
そこで、単純に僕が牛タン食べたかったのもありまして...
Also, I simply just wanted to eat beef tongue...

613
00:47:22,519 --> 00:47:25,819
アンケートを書いた時にね。なので今回、牛タンを選ばせていただきました。
when filling out the questionnaire. So this time, I selected beef tongue.

614
00:47:25,819 --> 00:47:29,519
確かに！美味しくならないわけがない！
Indeed! There's no way it won't be delicious!

615
00:47:29,519 --> 00:47:31,519
なるほどですね。
I see.

616
00:47:31,519 --> 00:47:33,819
確かに焼肉系は上手そう！
Certainly, barbecue-style food sounds delicious!

617
00:47:33,819 --> 00:47:44,219
Gyutan which is beef tongue, it is a yakiniku meat, and the reason he chose it was because, well, it's meat, Vegemite is salty, would be a good pairing, one would think. なるほどですね。
Gyutan which is beef tongue, it is a yakiniku meat, and the reason he chose it was because, well, it's meat, Vegemite is salty, would be a good pairing, one would think. I see.

618
00:47:44,219 --> 00:47:46,119
はい。素晴らしい！
Yes. Wonderful!

619
00:47:46,119 --> 00:47:50,919
これはお互いプロの方にお願いしているので...
Since we asked a professional to handle this...

620
00:47:50,919 --> 00:47:53,719
何が出てくるでしょうか！
what will come out, I wonder!

621
00:47:53,719 --> 00:47:56,619
ドキドキするな、これ。
This is getting nerve-wracking.

622
00:47:56,619 --> 00:47:59,719
じゃあ、見ていきましょう！おねがいします！
Well then, let's take a look! Here we go!

623
00:47:59,719 --> 00:48:02,619
うわー！おいしそう！
Woah! That looks so delicious!

624
00:48:02,619 --> 00:48:05,619
うまそうだけど...めちゃめちゃ旨そう！
It looks tasty, but... it looks insanely delicious!

625
00:48:05,619 --> 00:48:09,619
うっまそー！えっ、ちょっと待って、ベジマイトを発見できないですよね、ちょっと...
Looks so good! Wait, you can't really spot the Vegemite, can you? A bit...

626
00:48:09,619 --> 00:48:12,719
え、すごい！どこか入ってる？
Eh, amazing! Is it in there somewhere?

627
00:48:12,719 --> 00:48:17,519
これがね、一応「牛タン トルティーヤ」。
This is, for now, "Beef Tongue Tortilla".

628
00:48:17,519 --> 00:48:19,519
トルティーヤ！ It's like a tortilla, it's like a wrap!
Tortilla! It's like a tortilla, it's like a wrap!

629
00:48:19,519 --> 00:48:21,119
はいはいはいはい。
Right, right, right.

630
00:48:21,119 --> 00:48:23,819
最近はね、タコスも流行ってますから。
Tacos have been popular lately, after all.

631
00:48:23,819 --> 00:48:27,819
It's like this really... Yeah, ソースめちゃいい匂いするっすね。
It's like this really... Yeah, the sauce smells really nice.

632
00:48:27,819 --> 00:48:29,919
ソースをかけたらいいのかな、これは？
Should we pour the sauce on it?

633
00:48:29,919 --> 00:48:32,019
じゃあちょっと食べてみます。
Well, let me try eating it.

634
00:48:32,019 --> 00:48:33,519
食べてみます。
Let me try it too.

635
00:48:33,519 --> 00:48:35,419
ロベルさん、いっちゃってよ！
Roberu-san, go for it!

636
00:48:35,419 --> 00:48:37,419
ちゃんとしてるな！すごい！いただきます！
It's properly made! Amazing! Bon appétit!

637
00:48:37,419 --> 00:48:40,119
ちゃんとして...
Properly...

638
00:48:40,119 --> 00:48:42,619
お！いってるいってるいってる！
Oh! He's eating it, eating it!

639
00:48:42,619 --> 00:48:45,419
じゃあ僕も、いただきまーす！
Then I'll eat too! Bon appétit!

640
00:48:45,419 --> 00:48:48,919
お、いい感じだぞ、ロベルさんが。
Oh, Roberu-san looks like he's enjoying it.

641
00:48:48,919 --> 00:48:53,119
ロベさんどうよ？
Robe-san, how is it?

642
00:48:53,119 --> 00:48:57,119
いや、あのね...言っていっすか？
Well, you know... can I say it?

643
00:48:57,119 --> 00:49:00,119
全然美味しいっす！
It's completely delicious!

644
00:49:00,119 --> 00:49:03,519
ベジマイトがどこにいるかわかんないっす！
I can't tell where the Vegemite is!

645
00:49:03,519 --> 00:49:06,919
え、それは合ってるの？
Wait, is that supposed to happen?

646
00:49:06,919 --> 00:49:08,819
わかんないっす！
I don't know!

647
00:49:08,819 --> 00:49:11,819
ベーさんも美味い？
Is it good to you too, Bae?

648
00:49:11,819 --> 00:49:13,919
美味い！
It's delicious!

649
00:49:13,919 --> 00:49:16,919
今、2人が先に食べてリアクション見てから食べようと思って。
I thought I'd watch you two eat and react first before trying it.

650
00:49:16,919 --> 00:49:18,119
ありがとう！
Thank you!

651
00:49:18,119 --> 00:49:20,219
じゃあ大丈夫そうだね。いただきます！
Looks like it's safe then. Bon appétit!

652
00:49:20,219 --> 00:49:28,119
こいつ...うっま！
This... is so delicious!

653
00:49:28,119 --> 00:49:31,019
うまい！
Delicious!

654
00:49:31,019 --> 00:49:35,519
本当にね、ベジマイトがどこにいるかマジで分からん！
Seriously, I really can't tell where the Vegemite is!

655
00:49:35,519 --> 00:49:40,119
これ、これはまたプロの方からのあれがあるんですかね？
Is there a comment from the professional for this dish?

656
00:49:40,119 --> 00:49:44,819
We have a comment from the food coordinator.

657
00:49:44,819 --> 00:49:49,119
牛タンというのは、塩レモンダレでよく食べるところから発想いたしました。
The idea came from how beef tongue is often eaten with salt lemon sauce.

658
00:49:49,119 --> 00:49:55,819
レモン塩ダレの塩部分をベジマイトにしました。
I replaced the salt part of the lemon salt sauce with Vegemite.

659
00:49:55,819 --> 00:50:00,119
The idea came from the way beef tongue is commonly enjoyed with a salted lemon sauce, so instead of salt...

660
00:50:00,134 --> 00:50:01,600
salt in the lemon sauce, we replaced it with Vegemite!

661
00:50:03,134 --> 00:50:04,334
天才すぎる！
You're too much of a genius!

662
00:50:04,667 --> 00:50:07,900
あ、そう？ なるほど、塩味だけを残したんだ。
Oh really? I see, so they kept just the saltiness.

663
00:50:08,667 --> 00:50:11,000
でもベジマイトの風味はあまりないですか？
But isn't there much Vegemite flavor?

664
00:50:11,134 --> 00:50:13,300
あ、確かに食べ終わった後ちょっと...
Ah, true, after eating it, a little bit...

665
00:50:13,334 --> 00:50:16,934
It has like a slight like, it's like a refreshing breeze of Vegemite!

666
00:50:17,567 --> 00:50:19,600
なんか優しい風みたいな。
Like a gentle breeze.

667
00:50:19,600 --> 00:50:21,067
確かにね。
True.

668
00:50:21,200 --> 00:50:24,167
ベジマイトが優しい風になることあるんだね。
So Vegemite can become a gentle breeze!

669
00:50:24,167 --> 00:50:25,567
そうです！
That's right!

670
00:50:25,734 --> 00:50:29,934
ベジマイトだけ食べたら岩で殴られたみたいな衝撃あったけど、
Eating Vegemite plain felt like getting hit with a rock,

671
00:50:29,934 --> 00:50:33,534
こんな優しい風に調理できるんだね、ベジマイトってね。
but it's impressive it can be cooked into such a gentle breeze.

672
00:50:33,534 --> 00:50:35,167
ベジマイトは優しいです。
Vegemite is gentle.

673
00:50:35,167 --> 00:50:37,867
スゴ！ これ美味しいですね。
Amazing! This is delicious, isn't it?

674
00:50:38,334 --> 00:50:41,134
では続いて、石川さん！
Now then, next up, Ishikawa-san!

675
00:50:41,534 --> 00:50:46,000
We gonna move on with Ishikawa Kaito-san's ingredient.

676
00:50:46,167 --> 00:50:47,867
やりましょう！ どんなものを選びました？
Let's do this! What kind of item did you choose?

677
00:50:48,200 --> 00:50:52,567
じゃあ僕が選んだ食材、こちらです！ドン！
Well then, the ingredient I chose is this! Bam!

678
00:50:52,567 --> 00:50:54,134
何？ 何ですか？
What is it?

679
00:50:54,134 --> 00:50:56,167
納豆です！
It's natto!

680
00:50:56,167 --> 00:51:02,434
イヤーーー！ 来たーーー！ 納豆！ キッツ！
Nooo! It's here! Natto! Harsh!

681
00:51:03,200 --> 00:51:05,767
あれ、納豆好き？ / 納豆好きよ！ / ですよね。
Wait, do you like natto? / I like natto! / Right.

682
00:51:06,134 --> 00:51:08,667
もうクセ強にはクセ強をぶつけたら、
I thought if you hit a strong flavor with another strong flavor,

683
00:51:08,667 --> 00:51:11,900
こう何だろう、相乗効果みたいのするんじゃないかなと思って。
they'd create synergy or something.

684
00:51:12,300 --> 00:51:14,467
I like the way he thinks! I like the way he thinks!

685
00:51:14,534 --> 00:51:16,667
もうめちゃくちゃ素晴らしいと思います。
I think that's super wonderful.

686
00:51:16,667 --> 00:51:20,600
そう、こちらを選ばせていただきました。日本の文化をぶつけてやるぜ！
Yes, that's why I chose this. I'm gonna hit it with Japanese culture!

687
00:51:21,134 --> 00:51:23,834
This is Japanese culture! Yes!

688
00:51:24,134 --> 00:51:27,834
Well, without further ado, what is the professional chef gonna do this time?

689
00:51:27,834 --> 00:51:30,200
見ていきましょう！ お願いします！
Let's take a look! Please show us!

690
00:51:30,334 --> 00:51:32,067
どうなっちゃうの、納豆は？
What's gonna happen to the natto?

691
00:51:32,534 --> 00:51:37,534
おー！ えー！？ なんだこれ！？ どういうこと！？
Woah! Huh!? What is this!? What does this mean!?

692
00:51:38,334 --> 00:51:42,200
うまそう！ え、何何何？ どういう食べ物...？
Looks delicious! Wait, what is it? What kind of food...?

693
00:51:42,200 --> 00:51:45,834
あの、発酵生春巻き？ / 発酵生春巻き！
Um, Fermented Fresh Spring Rolls? / Fermented Fresh Spring Rolls!

694
00:51:46,200 --> 00:51:50,534
生春巻きだ！ 発酵生春巻きって言葉も初めて聞きましたけど...
It's fresh spring rolls! I've never even heard the phrase 'fermented fresh spring rolls' before...

695
00:51:51,234 --> 00:51:53,167
うわ、めっちゃトロトロしてる！
Woah, it's super slimy!

696
00:51:53,500 --> 00:51:55,900
これもう一口でいくか。 / いっちゃってよ、Baeさん。
Should we take it in one bite? / Go ahead, Bae-san.

697
00:51:56,134 --> 00:51:58,900
じゃ、つけていただきます。
Then, I'll dip it and eat.

698
00:51:59,134 --> 00:52:04,334
うわ、めっちゃ... It's so slimy. いただきます！
Woah, so... It's so slimy. Bon appetit!

699
00:52:04,334 --> 00:52:07,900
ん？ え、これ...
Hmm? Wait, this...

700
00:52:11,200 --> 00:52:15,067
カイトさん。 / え？ / 先に言っておく。 / うん。
Kaito-san. / Eh? / I'll tell you in advance. / Yeah.

701
00:52:15,134 --> 00:52:17,767
明確に『いる』。 / いる？
It's distinctly 'there'. / 'There'?

702
00:52:18,134 --> 00:52:24,534
いる！ ...奴がいる。
It's there! That guy is in there.

703
00:52:26,634 --> 00:52:31,067
いるなー！ いるー！
It's definitely there!

704
00:52:31,134 --> 00:52:35,467
いやこれ、ソースにいるね。 / ソースか！ / うん。
No, wait, it's in the sauce. / It's the sauce?! / Yeah.

705
00:52:35,667 --> 00:52:40,067
あれ？ 全然味しないんですけど。 / え？ ん？ / うまい！
Huh? I can't taste it at all though. / Eh? Huh? / It's delicious!

706
00:52:40,134 --> 00:52:44,867
え！？ あれ、チェンジした？ / いや、いるよ！ / え？
What!? Wait, did it change? / No, it's there! / Eh?

707
00:52:45,134 --> 00:52:48,200
あれが納豆に押しかけてるぐらいまだある。
It's so strong it's almost pushing back against the natto.

708
00:52:48,200 --> 00:52:50,834
うん、わかる。相当だね。 / めっちゃ美味しい！
Yeah, I know. It's quite something. / It's super delicious!

709
00:52:50,834 --> 00:52:54,767
うん、美味しい。普通に。 / 発酵同士なので相性が良いとのことでございます。
Yeah, it's delicious. Normally. / Since both are fermented, they go well together.

710
00:52:55,334 --> 00:53:00,067
やっぱ塩味があるので何かのソースにできるとやっぱ塩味なんですね。
Because of the saltiness, if you make it into a sauce, it brings out that saltiness.

711
00:53:00,134 --> 00:53:05,934
納豆のタレ、なるほど納豆のタレをベジマイトにしたらいいなと思い、マヨベースにしてその中にベジマイト入りタレを作りました。
"The natto sauce—I thought it'd be good to make the natto sauce with Vegemite, so I made a mayonnaise-based sauce mixed with Vegemite."

712
00:53:08,634 --> 00:53:11,000
おー！ なるほど！
Oh! I see!

713
00:53:11,234 --> 00:53:16,234
So, Vegemite's really nice and salty. I figured it could work as a base for sauce. Had the idea of replacing the sauce that comes with natto with Vegemite...

714
00:53:16,234 --> 00:53:20,767
Made a mayonnaise-based sauce and mixed Vegemite into it!

715
00:53:21,067 --> 00:53:25,934
うまい！ 食えちゃうんだよね！ / まあね！
It's good! You can actually eat it! / Well, yeah!

716
00:53:26,634 --> 00:53:31,867
普通に美味しいです。 / This is so good. Oh my god. もうキラキラ！
It's plain delicious. / This is so good. Oh my god. It's glowing!

717
00:53:32,134 --> 00:53:37,667
最後に行きますが... / はい。 / 食後の...
Moving on to the last one... / Yes. / After the meal...

718
00:53:37,734 --> 00:53:41,334
何笑ってんの、おい！ 何ヘラヘラしてんの？
What are you laughing at, hey! Why are you smirking?

719
00:53:41,334 --> 00:53:45,900
食後ってふつう何食べております？ / あ、食後の後？ / はい！ / ま、デザートみたいな。
What do you usually eat after a meal? / Ah, after a meal? / Yes! / Well, like dessert.

720
00:53:45,900 --> 00:53:51,734
デザートですね！ 次は僕が選んだ食べ物になります。 / はい。
Dessert, right! Next is the food item I chose. / Yes.

721
00:53:52,134 --> 00:53:58,867
We have reached the final dish. And normally at the end of every meal, you do have dessert. Australia...

722
00:53:58,867 --> 00:54:05,867
トレジャー... ２つを組んだらどうなるか... / 宝物を２つ？
Treasures... What happens when you combine two of them... / Two treasures?

723
00:54:05,867 --> 00:54:11,067
宝物２つを組んだらどうなっちゃうか、ちょっとめちゃくちゃ気になったんで...
I was really curious about what would happen if you combined two treasures...

724
00:54:11,134 --> 00:54:18,134
えっと、最後の... 材料はこちらになります！ / 何？ 怖っ！
Um, the final... ingredient is this! / What? Terrifying!

725
00:54:18,634 --> 00:54:25,900
ティムタムです！ / 誰？ 何？ ティムタムは？ その宝物知らないわ！
It's Tim Tams! / Who? What? Tim Tam? I don't know that treasure!

726
00:54:26,134 --> 00:54:29,134
え、ティムタム知らないっすか？ / 知らないよ！
Eh, you don't know Tim Tam? / I don't!

727
00:54:29,434 --> 00:54:36,667
これはオーストラリアのめちゃくちゃ有名なチョコレート、ビスケット... / あーなるほど！ あれね！
This is Australia's super famous chocolate biscuit... / Ah, I see! That one!

728
00:54:36,667 --> 00:54:40,067
ティムタムです。 / ティムタムってお菓子ね！ / お菓子です！
It's Tim Tam. / Tim Tam is a snack! / It's a snack!

729
00:54:40,134 --> 00:54:46,167
それをじゃあくれるんだ！ その、ベジマイトとかじゃなくて、単体でね。お土産でね。
So you're giving that to us! Not with Vegemite, but by itself. As a souvenir!

730
00:54:46,167 --> 00:54:52,067
美味しいんだろうね！ ありがとう、クッキー、ビスケットは！ 本当に呼んでくれてありがとう、今日は！
Must be delicious! Thanks for the cookies/biscuits! Thanks so much for inviting us today!

731
00:54:52,134 --> 00:54:54,467
ご褒美だよね！ 頑張った俺たちに対する！
It's a reward! For us who worked hard!

732
00:54:54,634 --> 00:55:00,134
ということで、プロの方だったら、ティムタム＋ベジマイト...
So, if it's a professional chef, Tim Tam + Vegemite...

733
00:55:00,149 --> 00:55:03,649
...美味しく作ってくれたのかなって...
...if they made it delicious for us...

734
00:55:03,949 --> 00:55:05,649
なんで混ぜんだよ！
Why did you mix them?!

735
00:55:05,649 --> 00:55:07,649
...思いましたので...
...so I thought...

736
00:55:07,649 --> 00:55:12,949
You know, as a pro chef, I wanted to see what they can do, and I believe in their skills as a pro chef.

737
00:55:12,949 --> 00:55:15,149
みんな行きましょう！お願いします！
Let's go, everyone! Please!

738
00:55:15,649 --> 00:55:18,149
おっとっとっと…
Whoa, whoa, whoa...

739
00:55:18,149 --> 00:55:20,149
どういうこと？ティラミス？
What do you mean? Tiramisu?

740
00:55:20,149 --> 00:55:21,949
ティラミスじゃん！
It's tiramisu!

741
00:55:21,949 --> 00:55:24,149
え、うまっ…え？どういうこと？
Huh, looks good... Huh? What's going on?

742
00:55:24,649 --> 00:55:29,949
まあ、ちょっと一旦、発案者だしさ、先に食べてみてよ。 / はい、いただきます！
Well, since she came up with it, let her try it first. / Thanks for the food!

743
00:55:29,949 --> 00:55:35,149
え、でもなんか…めちゃくちゃ美味しそう…すごいなー！
Wait, but it looks... so delicious. That's amazing!

744
00:55:35,149 --> 00:55:38,149
うわー！これがベジマイト入ってる？いただきます。
Wow! Does this really have Vegemite in it? Bon appétit.

745
00:55:37,649 --> 00:55:41,349
いや、わからん。警戒心が強くなりすぎてるだけかもしれん。
I don't know, maybe we're just being way too cautious.

746
00:55:41,349 --> 00:55:45,149
普通にティラミスじゃん。
It's just a normal tiramisu.

747
00:55:45,149 --> 00:55:48,149
いただきます！
Bon appétit!

748
00:55:53,149 --> 00:55:56,649
なんか不思議そうな顔してない？
Doesn't she look a bit puzzled?

749
00:55:56,649 --> 00:55:58,649
あれ？本当に入ってます？ベジマイト。
Wait, is Vegemite really in here?

750
00:55:59,149 --> 00:56:02,649
え？入ってそうですよ？ / 美味しい！
Huh? Looks like it's in there. / Delicious!

751
00:56:02,649 --> 00:56:08,649
え？普通にティラミスやん。 / いただきます。
Huh? It's just normal tiramisu. / Bon appétit.

752
00:56:08,649 --> 00:56:15,149
ベーちゃんが一番分かってないまであるからな、ベジマイト。
Bae might actually be the one who understands Vegemite the least.

753
00:56:16,149 --> 00:56:19,649
マジで？え？ベジマイトがいるのか？
Seriously? Huh? Is Vegemite actually in there?

754
00:56:19,649 --> 00:56:23,949
確かに塩気あってうまっ！あ、いるわ！
There's definitely a salty taste and it's good! Ah, it's there!

755
00:56:23,949 --> 00:56:27,149
いる！え、うまっ！え、美味しい！
It's there! Wow, it's good! It's delicious!

756
00:56:27,149 --> 00:56:30,149
めっちゃうまいんだけどこれ！うま！
This is insanely good! So good!

757
00:56:30,149 --> 00:56:32,149
Oh my god!

758
00:56:32,649 --> 00:56:38,149
これお店出しましょう。 / We need a copyright, we need a patent, oh my god!
We should open a shop for this. / We need a copyright, we need a patent, oh my god!

759
00:56:38,149 --> 00:56:46,149
えー、ティムタムと合う料理は思いつくのが大変でした。すみませんでした！本当に！
"Uh, coming up with a dish that pairs with Tim Tams was really tough. I'm sorry! Truly!"

760
00:56:46,149 --> 00:56:51,649
ティムタム自体コーヒーが合いそうだと思ったのでティラミスにしました。
"I thought coffee would go well with Tim Tams, so I made tiramisu."

761
00:56:51,649 --> 00:56:58,149
ティムタムのクッキーはサクサク感を活かしたいので、ティムタムを砕いてベジマイトを…
"To keep the crunchy texture of the Tim Tam, I crushed the Tim Tams and..."

762
00:56:58,149 --> 00:57:05,649
ティムタムを砕いて、その中にベジマイト入れて、混ぜて、それをやってるんだ。
Crushing Tim Tams, putting Vegemite in it, mixing it up, and that's how it's made.

763
00:57:05,649 --> 00:57:16,149
Apparently it was really hard to think of a dish that would pair well with Tim Tam, but Tim Tam goes well with coffee! Decided to make a tiramisu! Also wanted to keep the crunchy texture of the Tim Tam, so I crushed it up, soaked it with Vegemite...

764
00:57:16,149 --> 00:57:20,149
すッげえうまい！
It's insanely good!

765
00:57:20,149 --> 00:57:23,149
しかも、普通のティラミスより美味しくなってて。 / でしょー！
Plus, it actually tastes better than a normal tiramisu. / Right?!

766
00:57:23,149 --> 00:57:27,149
塩気がいい味出してる。甘みが際立つというか。
The saltiness brings out a great flavor. It really highlights the sweetness.

767
00:57:27,149 --> 00:57:34,149
でかつ生クリームの濃さとかが塩気によってちょっと中和される感もあって、めちゃくちゃくどくない。
And the richness of the heavy cream gets neutralized by the saltiness, so it's not heavy at all.

768
00:57:34,149 --> 00:57:36,149
ねー！ / うまい！
Right?! / Delicious!

769
00:57:36,149 --> 00:57:46,149
ティラミスにすることによってコーヒーの香りと苦味で、ティムタムのすっごい甘い感じも程よくまろやかになって…
By making it a tiramisu, the coffee aroma and bitterness smooth out the intense sweetness of the Tim Tam nicely...

770
00:57:46,149 --> 00:57:51,149
これさ、ティムタムがうまいんじゃないの？
Isn't it just that Tim Tams are delicious?

771
00:57:51,149 --> 00:57:56,149
でも！ティムタムの美味しさをちょっとね、昇華させたの！もうベジマイトのおかげなんで！
But! It elevated the taste of the Tim Tam! It's all thanks to Vegemite!

772
00:57:56,149 --> 00:58:01,149
All because of Vegemite, Tim Tam's deliciousness has been, you know... / これうまっ！
All because of Vegemite, Tim Tam's deliciousness has been, you know... / This is so good!

773
00:58:01,149 --> 00:58:08,649
すごいわ。プロってすごいな。あのベジマイトをこんなにできるの？
Pros are incredible. How can they transform that Vegemite into this?

774
00:58:08,649 --> 00:58:12,149
「あのベジマイト」はやめてください！ / ごめんなさい！
Stop saying "that Vegemite"! / Sorry!

775
00:58:13,149 --> 00:58:18,149
めっちゃ食ってますね。よかったです。 / 完食です！
You're eating so much. I'm glad. / Cleaned the plate!

776
00:58:18,149 --> 00:58:23,649
あのね、全部うまかったな。総じて、今んとこ3個食べたけど。
You know, all of them were good overall. So far we've had three dishes.

777
00:58:23,649 --> 00:58:30,149
えーと、ちょっと最後に、美味しさっていうか、三つ星の評価っていうか、やりたくて。
Uh, lastly, I want to do a rating out of three stars for how delicious they were.

778
00:58:30,149 --> 00:58:36,149
I want to rate all of the different dishes. どれが一番美味しかったかちょっと決めたいので。
I want to rate all of the different dishes, to decide which one was the most delicious.

779
00:58:36,149 --> 00:58:42,149
今まで食べた中で、どれが一番ベジマイトと相性が良かったかってことね。なるほど。
Out of what we've eaten, which one paired best with Vegemite. Got it.

780
00:58:42,149 --> 00:58:45,149
じゃあまず、えっと、先輩の牛タンですね。
First, senior's beef tongue taco.

781
00:58:45,149 --> 00:58:50,149
何星ですか？ How many stars are we giving the Gyutan?
How many stars are we giving the beef tongue?

782
00:58:50,149 --> 00:58:55,649
俺は、二つ星かな。
For me, 2 stars.

783
00:58:55,649 --> 00:59:02,149
まあ、俺も2かな。 / 僕も2だと思いましたね。めちゃくちゃ美味しかったです。
I'd give it a 2 as well. / I thought 2 as well. It was super delicious.

784
00:59:02,149 --> 00:59:06,649
次が、フータさんの春巻きね。俺、1つ星かな！
Next is Fuuta's spring rolls. For me, 1 star!

785
00:59:06,649 --> 00:59:09,649
ごめん、俺も1つ星かな。
Sorry, I think 1 star for me too.

786
00:59:09,649 --> 00:59:13,649
自分は2.5なんですけど！あれ、めちゃくちゃ美味しい！
I'm giving it 2.5 though! What? It was super tasty!

787
00:59:13,649 --> 00:59:17,149
いや、美味しかったんだけど… / 美味しかった！ / ベジマイトがいた！
No, it was good, but... / It was good! / Vegemite was there!

788
00:59:17,149 --> 00:59:22,149
なんか風邪じゃなかった、ベジマイトが。まだ恋しいぐらいだった。
It wasn't just a trace, Vegemite was really present. A bit too noticeable.

789
00:59:22,149 --> 00:59:27,649
たしかにそうですね。あれが好きだったかもしれないです、自分は。
That's true. I might have actually liked that part.

790
00:59:27,649 --> 00:59:31,649
で、最後、僕のティラミス、ティムタム何星ですか？
And lastly, how many stars for my Tiramisu Tim Tam?

791
00:59:31,649 --> 00:59:35,149
3！ / 3！ / 僕も3！勝ったー！
3! / 3! / 3 for me too! I won!

792
00:59:35,149 --> 00:59:39,149
三つ星すぎ！
Solid 3 stars!

793
00:59:39,149 --> 00:59:44,149
ベジマイトがティムタムの甘さを活かしてた。 / ですよね！
The Vegemite actually highlighted the sweetness of the Tim Tam. / Right?!

794
00:59:44,149 --> 00:59:52,149
流石ベジマイトです。 / もうこのティラミスが、2つの宝が合わさったことによって、たった一つの大秘宝になってた！
As expected of Vegemite. / Combining these two treasures into a single grand treasure!

795
00:59:52,149 --> 00:59:55,149
あいつオーストラリアから何か貰おうとしてるな！
That guy's trying to get sponsored by Australia!

796
00:59:55,149 --> 00:59:59,149
僕アニメ声優をやってましてね！
I work as an anime voice actor, you know!

797
01:00:00,164 --> 01:00:01,064
すごく
Really...

798
01:00:01,164 --> 01:00:02,964
企画、まあ、こういう感じだったんですけど...
The plan was originally like this, but...

799
01:00:03,064 --> 01:00:06,764
ちょっとベジマイトの最初のイメージ変わりました。
...my initial image of Vegemite has changed a bit.

800
01:00:06,764 --> 01:00:07,964
あ、最初に食べてみてからっと。
Oh, compared to when you first tried it?

801
01:00:07,964 --> 01:00:11,064
感想、まあね、感想変わりました、もしかして。
Your, well, impression changed, perhaps?

802
01:00:11,264 --> 01:00:13,664
なんか物によってはというか...
Well, depending on what it's paired with...

803
01:00:13,764 --> 01:00:18,564
こんなにもやり方次第でベジマイトの味が変化していくものなのかとか...
...or how it's prepared, the flavor of Vegemite can change this much...

804
01:00:18,664 --> 01:00:22,064
なんか色々な使い方のがあるんだなって意味でびっくりはしたね。
I was really surprised by how many different ways there are to use it.

805
01:00:22,164 --> 01:00:24,864
うん、すごくびっくりしました、僕、ベジマイト。
Yeah, I was really surprised by Vegemite.

806
01:00:25,164 --> 01:00:27,164
ロベ先輩、ショック！好きになりました？
Robe-senpai is shocked! Did you end up liking it?

807
01:00:27,164 --> 01:00:27,864
はい。
Yes.

808
01:00:28,164 --> 01:00:29,464
好きになりました？
Did you come to like it?

809
01:00:29,464 --> 01:00:29,964
はい。
Yes.

810
01:00:29,964 --> 01:00:31,064
好きになりました？
Did you come to like it?

811
01:00:31,064 --> 01:00:32,564
はい、ありがとうございます。はい、ベジマイト...
Yes, thank you. Yes, Vegemite...

812
01:00:32,564 --> 01:00:35,064
I like Vegemite.

813
01:00:35,064 --> 01:00:35,964
いや、"like" じゃない。
No, not "like".

814
01:00:36,064 --> 01:00:37,864
I love Vegemite.

815
01:00:37,964 --> 01:00:39,164
あ、ありがとうございます！
Ah, thank you so much!

816
01:00:39,164 --> 01:00:39,864
Yeah.

817
01:00:39,864 --> 01:00:40,564
はい！
Yes!

818
01:00:40,664 --> 01:00:42,364
ありがとうございます！はい！
Thank you very much! Yes!

819
01:00:42,364 --> 01:00:43,864
で、界人さんは？
And how about you, Kaito-san?

820
01:00:43,864 --> 01:00:46,164
俺は、やっぱこう最初の印象は...
For me, my initial impression was...

821
01:00:46,264 --> 01:00:50,964
もういろんな味がすることで、こう、なんだろう、びっくりするな...
...like, having so many flavors hit at once makes you go, "Whoa..."

822
01:00:51,064 --> 01:00:52,364
なんか...
Like...

823
01:00:52,364 --> 01:00:53,164
みんなショックやん！
Everyone was in shock!

824
01:00:53,164 --> 01:00:54,764
...っていう印象だったんだけど...
...that was my impression, but...

825
01:00:54,764 --> 01:00:55,364
はい。
Yes.

826
01:00:55,464 --> 01:00:58,064
こんなに色んな調理の仕方すると...
...when you cook it in so many different ways...

827
01:00:58,164 --> 01:01:04,664
ベジマイトの色んな味がするっていういいところを、ちょっとずつこう、拾っていけるんだと思って。
...you can pick out the good aspects of Vegemite's complex flavor profile step by step.

828
01:01:04,864 --> 01:01:08,664
無限の可能性がある食材だという風に思いましたね。
I realized it's an ingredient with infinite possibilities.

829
01:01:08,664 --> 01:01:09,764
好きですか？好きになりました？
Do you like it? Did you come to like it?

830
01:01:10,064 --> 01:01:12,764
あー... いや、まあね...
Ah... Well, you know...

831
01:01:12,764 --> 01:01:13,664
好きになりました？
Did you come to like it?

832
01:01:13,664 --> 01:01:15,464
あの、あんまり俺、嘘...
Umm, I don't really like to lie...

833
01:01:15,464 --> 01:01:16,264
好きになりました？
Did you come to like it?

834
01:01:16,364 --> 01:01:17,464
Yes.

835
01:01:17,564 --> 01:01:18,164
え？
Eh?

836
01:01:18,164 --> 01:01:18,864
はい。
Yes.

837
01:01:18,864 --> 01:01:19,764
え？
Eh?

838
01:01:19,864 --> 01:01:21,264
好きになりました？
Did you come to like it?

839
01:01:21,364 --> 01:01:23,064
はい！
YES!

840
01:01:23,164 --> 01:01:25,964
ざいます！
Thank you!

841
01:01:26,664 --> 01:01:27,864
えっーと、まあ...
Umm, well...

842
01:01:27,864 --> 01:01:32,564
みんなもね、気になったら、もうぜひぜひベジマイトを自分で買って、自分でちょっとね...
Everyone, if you're curious, please buy some Vegemite and try it yourself...

843
01:01:32,564 --> 01:01:36,564
調理技術に自信があれば...
If you're confident in your cooking skills...

844
01:01:36,664 --> 01:01:44,364
If you want to find your own ways to enjoy Vegemite, I feel like, you know, it'll be such a great experience.

845
01:01:44,364 --> 01:01:46,164
瓶はちょっと... 瓶はちょっと...
The jar on its own is a bit... The jar on its own is a bit...

846
01:01:46,164 --> 01:01:48,564
まあまあ何はともあれ、べーちゃん、本当にあの...
Well anyway, Bae-chan, really...

847
01:01:48,564 --> 01:01:49,364
あ、本当に...
Ah, really...

848
01:01:49,364 --> 01:01:51,164
マジで5周年おめでとう！
Seriously, congratulations on 5 years!

849
01:01:51,164 --> 01:01:52,664
おめでとうございます！
Congratulations!

850
01:01:52,664 --> 01:01:53,964
ライブ開催もね。
And on the live show too!

851
01:01:53,964 --> 01:01:54,764
ありがとうございます！
Thank you so much!

852
01:01:54,764 --> 01:01:55,364
おめでとう！
Congratulations!

853
01:01:55,364 --> 01:01:56,964
ありがとうございます！来てくださってありがとうございます！
Thank you so much! Thank you for coming today!

854
01:01:56,964 --> 01:01:57,764
頑張ってね。
Do your best!

855
01:01:57,764 --> 01:02:04,364
Thank you to the two of them for coming. I can't believe this is how I'm celebrating my 5th year anniversary, but I'm so glad it is.

856
01:02:04,464 --> 01:02:05,864
ありがとうございました！
Thank you very much!

857
01:02:05,864 --> 01:02:06,564
じゃ、せーの...
Okay, ready, set...

858
01:02:06,664 --> 01:02:10,964
おつベジマイト！
Otsu-Vegemite!

859
01:02:11,164 --> 01:02:12,564
三つ星！
Three stars!

860
01:02:12,564 --> 01:02:14,764
良い子は真似しないでね！
Good kids, don't try this at home!

861
01:02:19,964 --> 01:02:25,464
And with that, we're almost at the end of my anniversary stream!

862
01:02:25,664 --> 01:02:29,064
I hope you all had fun today!

863
01:02:29,064 --> 01:02:32,064
いや、もう、終わりたくないね！
Ah, man, I don't want it to end!

864
01:02:32,164 --> 01:02:34,564
本当に5周年ありがとうございました！
Thank you so much for 5 years!

865
01:02:34,564 --> 01:02:38,364
Thank you so much for all the support for 5 years!

866
01:02:38,364 --> 01:02:39,664
We're not done yet!

867
01:02:39,664 --> 01:02:42,664
まだね、おしらせ一事残ってます！
We still have one last announcement left!

868
01:02:42,664 --> 01:02:44,364
なと！
And that is!

869
01:02:44,364 --> 01:02:45,464
グッズが出ます！
Merchandise is coming out!

870
01:02:45,464 --> 01:02:48,464
We still have the last announcement! 5th Anniversary merch!

871
01:02:48,464 --> 01:02:51,764
We've got some really cool merch this time, too!

872
01:02:51,764 --> 01:02:52,864
Please check it out!

873
01:02:52,864 --> 01:02:53,464
どうぞ！
Here you go!

874
01:02:54,764 --> 01:02:59,964
5th anniversary merch, of course it had to be the Monochrome Dancer...

875
01:02:59,964 --> 01:03:03,564
...and Rat Dancer! This is the Best Oshi merch!

876
01:03:03,564 --> 01:03:05,864
This beautiful artwork was done by Hyde-sensei!

877
01:03:05,964 --> 01:03:08,864
Hyde-sensei に書いていただきました！
Hyde-sensei drew this for us!

878
01:03:08,964 --> 01:03:12,864
今回のグッズのテーマは、まあやっぱり今年発表したモノクロームダンサー衣装と...
The theme for this merch set, well, is of course the Monochrome Dancer outfit revealed this year...

879
01:03:12,864 --> 01:03:17,264
...バックダンサーの、まあ、お二人ですね！はい！
...and the back dancers, the two of them! Yes!

880
01:03:17,564 --> 01:03:21,064
Let's go through each item one by one!

881
01:03:21,164 --> 01:03:23,164
First up is this!

882
01:03:24,164 --> 01:03:29,064
First is the acrylic stand! "Best Oshi" Acrylic Stand!

883
01:03:29,064 --> 01:03:30,564
ベスト推しアクリルスタンドですね！
It's the "Best Oshi" acrylic stand!

884
01:03:30,564 --> 01:03:32,164
It's so cool!

885
01:03:32,164 --> 01:03:36,564
It features the amazing artwork that Hyde did, and I think it features... It's all the best oshi...

886
01:03:36,564 --> 01:03:40,164
まあ、ベスト推し僕ですよね！僕ですね！
Well, the best oshi is me, right? It's me!

887
01:03:40,464 --> 01:03:43,864
Yes, of course! The best oshi, everyone's favorite oshi is me!

888
01:03:48,364 --> 01:03:48,564
But it does have the two back dancers in the back cause I know you guys love them!

889
01:03:48,664 --> 01:03:54,764
I'm so obsessed with how it turned out! めっちゃかっこいい感じになったと思います！
I'm so obsessed with how it turned out! I think it turned out super cool!

890
01:03:55,064 --> 01:03:57,164
Next up is...

891
01:03:58,364 --> 01:04:02,164
The "Rat Dancer" Jacket!

892
01:04:02,564 --> 01:04:08,664
やっとですね！"Rat Dancer" Jacket is becoming official merch!
Finally! The "Rat Dancer" jacket is becoming official merch!

893
01:04:08,664 --> 01:04:10,764
グッズになりました、ジャケットが！
The jacket became official merch!

894
01:04:10,764 --> 01:04:12,764
いや、本当に素晴らしい！
Wow, it's really wonderful!

895
01:04:12,764 --> 01:04:16,564
We've made a few adjustments so it's comfortable and easy to wear in everyday life.

896
01:04:16,664 --> 01:04:24,864
ちょっとね、このジャケットは着用しやすいよ。ちょっと調整をしたんですけど、本当にかっこいいジャケットになったと思います！
Yeah, this jacket is really easy to wear. We made some tweaks, and I think it turned out to be a really cool jacket!

897
01:04:25,464 --> 01:04:33,464
なんとね、This time, the 5th Anniversary merch doesn't have as many items, just because I know there's a lot happening.
You know, this time, the 5th Anniversary merch doesn't have as many items, just because I know there's a lot happening.

898
01:04:33,464 --> 01:04:39,264
We've got the album, you know, and also we've got the live and everything, so it's only these two items.

899
01:04:39,264 --> 01:04:44,464
But if you pick up the complete merch set, you will also get THIS!

900
01:04:45,264 --> 01:04:55,164
You will get a replica sticker with a signature and an exclusive ASMR voice pack as a special bonus! Thank you so much for always supporting me!

901
01:04:55,164 --> 01:05:00,064
えーと、もしね、今回ちょっとね、色、たくさん告知とかお知せがあったんですけど...
Umm, if, well, today there were a lot of announcements and notifications...

902
01:05:00,179 --> 01:05:05,079
今回の、あの、5周年グッズは2点になります。
This time, the 5th anniversary merch set consists of two items.

903
01:05:05,079 --> 01:05:08,979
もしセット買ってくれている方に、えっと、複製サイン入りのステッカーと、
For those who buy the full set, as a bonus...

904
01:05:08,979 --> 01:05:13,979
ASMRボイスが特典についてきます！
...it comes with a replicated autograph sticker and an ASMR Voice Pack!

905
01:05:13,979 --> 01:05:17,479
The title of the voice pack is "Be my model!"

906
01:05:17,479 --> 01:05:20,579
We check out the sample of the Red Dancing Jacket together,

907
01:05:20,579 --> 01:05:26,679
and there's even a scene where we actually recorded using the real jacket sample, so I hope you'll give it a listen!

908
01:05:27,679 --> 01:05:31,579
えーっと、まあ、こちらのボイスのタイトルは「ボクのモデルになって！」
Um, well, the title of this voice pack is "Be my model!"

909
01:05:32,079 --> 01:05:36,679
先ほどね、紹介した、ジャケットのサンプルを使って、
Using the jacket sample I introduced earlier,

910
01:05:36,679 --> 01:05:43,879
一緒になんかね、ボイスのシチュエーションを作ったっていうか、収録しました。
we recorded a situation together for the voice pack.

911
01:05:44,379 --> 01:05:46,979
お恥ずかしがりながら、ぜひ聴いてて下さい。
Though I'm a bit embarrassed, please give it a listen!

912
01:05:47,579 --> 01:05:51,779
You can access the shop directly from YouTube, so be sure to check it out!

913
01:05:51,779 --> 01:05:55,879
YouTubeからショップへアクセスできるので、チェックしてください！
You can access the shop directly from YouTube, so please check it out!

914
01:05:56,379 --> 01:05:59,979
はい！ That was the actual final announcement.
Yes! That was the actual final announcement.

915
01:05:59,979 --> 01:06:05,879
But before I go, there's one more thing I wanted to do with you all.

916
01:06:05,879 --> 01:06:09,279
And in order to do that, I need to first...

917
01:06:09,279 --> 01:06:10,679
変身！
Transform!

918
01:06:16,979 --> 01:06:20,479
はい、アイドルベア来ました！
Okay, Idol Bae is here!

919
01:06:21,179 --> 01:06:26,179
I just wanted to sing one song before we end today's stream.

920
01:06:26,679 --> 01:06:30,579
I just want to say thank you so much for 5 years. I'll continue doing my best.

921
01:06:30,579 --> 01:06:36,379
Thank you so much for everything you've given me, and I will do my best.

922
01:06:36,979 --> 01:06:39,979
5年間本当にありがとうございました。
Thank you so much for these 5 years.

923
01:06:39,979 --> 01:06:43,479
ちょっと最後にね、1曲歌いたいなと思ってます。
I'd like to sing one last song at the end.

924
01:06:43,479 --> 01:06:48,479
気持ちを込めてこれからも頑張りたいと思いますので、最後に1曲聴いてください！
Putting my feelings into it, I want to keep doing my best, so please listen to this last song!

925
01:06:48,479 --> 01:06:50,179
Music, スタート！
Music, start!

926
01:07:04,179 --> 01:07:07,679
誇り高きアイドルだ！
A proud idol!

927
01:07:14,979 --> 01:07:19,579
私のこと知ってますか？ 可愛く見えてますか？
Do you know who I am? Do I look cute to you?

928
01:07:19,579 --> 01:07:25,679
私の歌どうだろうな うまく歌えてますか？
What do you think about my singing? Did I manage to sing well?

929
01:07:25,679 --> 01:07:31,679
衣装だとかメイクだとか 可愛く見えてますか？
My costume and makeup... Do I look cute wearing them?

930
01:07:31,679 --> 01:07:37,679
振付とかファンサとかも 喜んでもらえますか？
My dancing and fan service... Do they make you happy?

931
01:07:37,679 --> 01:07:43,579
手は冷たくなって 足は震える
My hands are getting cold, and my legs are shaking.

932
01:07:43,579 --> 01:07:49,079
それでも戦いたい アイドルだから
Even so, I still want to keep fighting because I'm an idol!

933
01:07:49,079 --> 01:07:51,779
バカにする奴は嫌いだ
I hate people who make fun of me!

934
01:07:51,779 --> 01:07:54,779
見下されるのも嫌いだ
I don't like to be looked down on either!

935
01:07:54,779 --> 01:08:00,779
“アイドルなんか”という言葉を 見てもいないくせに言うな
Don't say words like "just an idol" when you haven't even actually seen us!

936
01:08:00,779 --> 01:08:03,579
頑張りを当然と言うな
Don't take my hard work for granted!

937
01:08:03,579 --> 01:08:06,679
イメージとか強制するな
Don't force an image on me!

938
01:08:06,679 --> 01:08:13,379
“アイドルなんか”という言葉は この世で一番大嫌いだ
Words like "just an idol" are the one thing I hate most in this world!

939
01:08:24,179 --> 01:08:29,179
プライベート見えないから 分からないと思います
Because you can't see my private life, I don't think you'd know this side of me...

940
01:08:29,179 --> 01:08:34,679
性格とか悪い方です 騙しちゃっていますか？
My personality is actually pretty bad. Did I manage to fool you?

941
01:08:34,679 --> 01:08:40,679
でも本気です 本気なんです ありのままの私を
But it's the truth, I'm being serious! Please love me the way I am...

942
01:08:40,679 --> 01:08:46,679
好きになって 推して下さい それってワガママですか？
...and become my fan. Is that a selfish thing to ask?

943
01:08:46,679 --> 01:08:52,679
きっと可愛くない 全部分かってる
I'm sure that I'm not cute, I already knew it all.

944
01:08:52,679 --> 01:08:58,379
それでも好かれてたい アイドルだから
Even so, I still want to be liked because I'm an idol!

945
01:08:58,379 --> 01:09:00,979
皮肉言う奴は嫌いだ
I hate people who say sarcastic things!

946
01:09:00,979 --> 01:09:03,679
言い訳ばかりも嫌いだ
I hate people who keep making excuses too!

947
01:09:03,679 --> 01:09:09,679
“こんなもんか”という言葉を 軽々しく口にするな
Don't just say words like "is that all?" so lightly!

948
01:09:09,679 --> 01:09:12,579
勝手に限界決めるな
Don't just set limits on me!

949
01:09:12,579 --> 01:09:15,679
笑い者になんてするな
Don't make a fool out of me!

950
01:09:15,679 --> 01:09:21,979
“アイドルなんか”という言葉は この世で一番大嫌いだ
Words like "just an idol" are the one thing I hate most in this world!

951
01:09:21,979 --> 01:09:24,579
向かい風を切り裂け
Cutting through the headwinds...

952
01:09:24,579 --> 01:09:28,179
誇り高きアイドル
...a proud idol...

953
01:09:32,579 --> 01:09:35,179
目指そうぜ
Let's aim to be one!

954
01:09:39,179 --> 01:09:42,179
応援がなければ 活動できない
Without all the support, I can't do any work.

955
01:09:42,179 --> 01:09:45,179
好きな事ばかりじゃ 生きてはいけない
I can't live my life by doing only the things that I like.

956
01:09:45,179 --> 01:09:47,979
元気あげるはずが もらってばかりだし
Even though I'm supposed to give you energy, I continue to receive it instead...

957
01:09:47,979 --> 01:09:53,479
恩返しできる日まで 待ってて
Until the day I can repay you comes, wait for me!

958
01:09:53,479 --> 01:09:59,679
待っててね！ 12月、約束だ！
Wait for me, okay?! December, it's a promise!

959
01:10:03,194 --> 01:10:05,294
歓声が減っても
Even if the cheers fade,

960
01:10:05,294 --> 01:10:07,994
